#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0196-A expect=skipped domain=ADLBC
#note "MOVED from the parent by the R-5.25 split (top-level-or board wave 2, group J): the PARAMCD half now lives in this sibling, and the Fix #331 gate moved with it. PARAMCD is absent; a bare empty(PARAMCD) is TRUE on every row of an absent column (absent = all-missing) and nothing else in the Check restricts the rows, so the rule would flood -- the ruled disposition is Requirements.Variables.All [PARAMCD], an auditable SKIP naming PARAMCD, with the absence itself left to one presence rule. The parent PMDA-AD0196 (the PARAM half) now EXECUTES on this dataset instead of skipping - the split strictly widened coverage. If this EXECUTES (violation or silent pass), the gate has been removed -- escalate, do not rewrite. History, before Fix #330: PARAMCD is not declared; PARAM is present and populated. The rule has no Requirements.Variables gate, so it EXECUTES; the loader's derived guard (shipped form var_exists(\"PARAM\") and empty(PARAM) or var_exists(\"PARAMCD\") and empty(PARAMCD)) disarms the PARAMCD arm while the PARAM arm is satisfied - the two arms are guarded INDEPENDENTLY, so the PARAMCD arm folds FALSE, the PARAM arm stays UNKNOWN and the tree falls through to the row path instead of the bare-empty() broadcast TRUE. Pins that an absent required column is somebody else's rule, not this one's."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADLBC structure=BDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAM   type=Char
col AVAL    type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | Alanine | 2.5
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 | Albumin | 7.0
